# FigDown — figures as text. Spec: https://github.com/FigDown/figdown
#
# Regression fixture for backlog item 66 (`TYPED-BLOCK-TITLE-CANVAS`): a typed block's
# own title must join its canvas computation. This is deliberately the
# smallest possible bitfield — two fields, one byte — under a title chosen to
# be far wider than the data, the shape the downstream report's own repro
# used (severity scales INVERSELY with figure size). Not a documentation
# example: gate:layout is the
# only reader of this file (see package.json's gate:layout script), so it
# stays outside examples/reference-coverage, cite-check and the other
# corpus-quality gates scoped to examples/ and figures/, none of which this
# fixture is trying to satisfy.
#
# Reverting `TYPED-BLOCK-TITLE-CANVAS` (drop the `typedBlockTitleW` union in `renderBitfield`'s
# return) makes this fixture's title run off the canvas at x<0 and turns
# `gate:layout --strict`'s offcv axis red on it. With `TYPED-BLOCK-TITLE-CANVAS` in place it scores
# offcv=0.

figdown 0.1 bitfield

bitfield tb "IPv4/IPv6 DS field (the old ToS byte) — RFC 2474 + RFC 3168" word=8 numbering=msb0
field "DSCP" 6
field "ECN" 2
